From 51df350bfdda3bdd2ff60ab5028313f5e3aa6e98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:09:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings: the Spanish files of Estuary translate the help of
 "Colour format" as it is in English now

The help of videoscreen.hadescolorformat (Estuary 32911) gained "and NVIDIA graphics
with driver 620 on HDMI, which has no 4:2:0" (020e9c0). Its translations in es_es, es_ar
and es_mx say it, but their msgid, the English they translate, was left as before: a
translator or a tool that compares them takes the translation for one of an older text.

The msgid of the three is the English of en_gb. Nothing that is shown changes.

Host test (outside the tree): msgidsync.py checks that every entry of the Spanish files
of Estuary that is new or changed since the base of this version translates the English
of en_gb, has a translation, and that none is missing; before, these three differ; after,
nothing.
---
 addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po | 2 +-
 addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po | 2 +-
 addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po
index 8425b64..cbaa85e 100644
--- a/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po
+++ b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po
@@ -3269,7 +3269,7 @@ msgstr "Formato de color"
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 #. Setting help: videoscreen.hadescolorformat (core #41311)
 msgctxt "#32911"
-msgid "The colour format that the graphics card sends to the display, where the driver lets Kodi choose it (AMD graphics). Automatic is what LibreELEC Hades does without this setting. A format that the driver cannot carry in a mode (for example YCbCr 4:4:4 at 3840x2160 and 60 Hz over HDMI 2.0) goes out as Automatic in that mode, and the log says so. Dolby Vision always goes out as RGB at 8 bits. Applies with the next change of mode, or the next video that signals HDR."
+msgid "The colour format that the graphics card sends to the display, where the driver lets Kodi choose it (AMD graphics, and NVIDIA graphics with driver 620 on HDMI, which has no 4:2:0). Automatic is what LibreELEC Hades does without this setting. A format that the driver cannot carry in a mode (for example YCbCr 4:4:4 at 3840x2160 and 60 Hz over HDMI 2.0) goes out as Automatic in that mode, and the log says so. Dolby Vision always goes out as RGB at 8 bits. Applies with the next change of mode, or the next video that signals HDR."
 msgstr "El formato de color que la tarjeta gráfica envía a la pantalla, donde el controlador deja que Kodi lo elija (gráficas AMD, y NVIDIA con el controlador 620 por HDMI, que no tiene 4:2:0). Automático es lo que hace LibreELEC Hades sin este ajuste. Un formato que el controlador no puede llevar en un modo (por ejemplo YCbCr 4:4:4 a 3840x2160 y 60 Hz por HDMI 2.0) sale como Automático en ese modo, y el registro lo dice. Dolby Vision siempre sale en RGB de 8 bits. Se aplica con el siguiente cambio de modo o el siguiente vídeo que señale HDR."
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
